# One natural-language command, e.g. "go to the red box, then come back".
#
# Why an ACTION and not a service: a command can take minutes (driving, searching),
# the user wants progress while it runs, and must be able to cancel it mid-way.
# Services give none of that; actions give all three (goal / feedback / result + cancel).

# ---- Goal: what the user asked
string command
# true = only parse and validate the command into a plan; do not move the robot
bool dry_run
---
# ---- Result: how it ended
bool success
# Human-readable summary: what was done, or why it failed / what needs clarifying
string message
# The validated plan that was (or would have been) executed, as JSON
string plan_json
# Which language backend produced the plan, e.g. "ollama:qwen2.5:7b-instruct" or "rules"
string backend
# Time the language layer took to produce the plan (seconds)
float32 parse_time_s
---
# ---- Feedback: progress while it runs
# parsing | executing | searching | step_done | done
string status
int32 step_index
int32 total_steps
# One-line description of the step in progress, e.g. "navigate to kitchen"
string current_step
